1
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:04,540
You're here.

2
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:07,380
Your organs are failing.

3
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:09,300
And your death is drawing near.

4
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:13,440
But if you bribe the right politicians in the right order at the right time,

5
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:16,600
you can trade the nuclear warheads for medicine.

6
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:20,080
And it's not even a crime.

7
00:01:40,384 --> 00:01:45,424
Recruitment and Propaganda Plan You want to end war and disease but don't

8
00:01:45,424 --> 00:01:48,974
have a nonprofit, a bank account, or anything to offer anyone.

9
00:01:49,524 --> 00:01:52,984
Here's how to recruit one hundred thousand humans before you have anything

10
00:01:52,984 --> 00:01:54,184
except an argument.

11
00:01:54,904 --> 00:01:59,544
It's a Kickstarter where the reward tier is 'possibly not dying,' which

12
00:01:59,544 --> 00:02:02,114
is the most compelling crowdfunding offer in history.

13
00:02:02,644 --> 00:02:03,984
Phase zero:

14
00:02:04,044 --> 00:02:06,644
Collecting Humans Before You Have Anything to Offer Them

15
00:02:07,464 --> 00:02:12,184
On Wishonia, if someone discovered everyone was dying from preventable causes,

16
00:02:12,664 --> 00:02:15,424
they would simply stop dying from preventable causes.

17
00:02:16,164 --> 00:02:20,804
On Earth, you need a tax-exempt entity, a bank account, and written permission

18
00:02:20,804 --> 00:02:23,704
from something called the Securities and Exchange Commission

19
00:02:24,364 --> 00:02:25,524
before you're allowed to try.

20
00:02:26,364 --> 00:02:30,404
The Securities and Exchange Commission regulates securities, which are financial

21
00:02:30,404 --> 00:02:34,104
instruments, not the kind of security where people stop dying.

22
00:02:34,644 --> 00:02:36,024
That would be a different department.

23
00:02:37,024 --> 00:02:37,864
You don't have that department.

24
00:02:39,224 --> 00:02:40,724
So you can't accept money yet.

25
00:02:41,124 --> 00:02:42,264
You can't sell bonds yet.

26
00:02:42,884 --> 00:02:46,304
You can't do anything that involves the movement of small pieces of paper.

27
00:02:47,124 --> 00:02:49,384
What you CAN do is collect names.

28
00:02:50,284 --> 00:02:54,864
The goal of Phase zero is building a database of every human who agrees

29
00:02:54,864 --> 00:02:58,804
that dying from preventable causes is a strange thing to tolerate.

30
00:02:59,524 --> 00:03:03,304
It's a Kickstarter where the reward tier is "possibly not dying,"

31
00:03:04,204 --> 00:03:08,544
which is the most compelling crowdfunding offer in history, and yet somehow

32
00:03:08,544 --> 00:03:09,964
requires marketing.

33
00:03:11,164 --> 00:03:13,244
The Bureaucratic Nesting Doll Problem.

34
00:03:14,244 --> 00:03:18,084
On your planet, before you can accept donations, you need five-oh-one c

35
00:03:18,084 --> 00:03:18,824
three status.

36
00:03:19,484 --> 00:03:22,224
Before you can sell bonds, you need S.E.C.

37
00:03:22,264 --> 00:03:22,764
registration.

38
00:03:23,024 --> 00:03:25,384
Before you can do either, you need a bank account.

39
00:03:26,204 --> 00:03:28,824
Before you can open a bank account, you need an organization.

40
00:03:29,984 --> 00:03:31,364
Before you can have an organization,

41
00:03:32,164 --> 00:03:32,924
you need the bank account.

42
00:03:34,164 --> 00:03:38,424
It's like a door that requires a key that's locked inside the room the door

43
00:03:38,424 --> 00:03:39,204
opens to.

44
00:03:40,024 --> 00:03:42,544
Your species built this system on purpose.

45
00:03:43,704 --> 00:03:48,104
The solution is the same one humans have used every time this has happened,

46
00:03:48,444 --> 00:03:50,004
which is every time.

47
00:03:50,724 --> 00:03:54,424
You collect people first, then point at the crowd when the institutions

48
00:03:54,424 --> 00:03:55,984
ask "but who wants this?".

49
00:03:57,264 --> 00:03:59,534
Abolition started with a list of names.

50
00:03:59,704 --> 00:04:01,184
Suffrage started with a list of names.

51
00:04:01,764 --> 00:04:03,664
Civil rights started with a list of names.

52
00:04:04,484 --> 00:04:06,384
Someone wrote down who agreed.

53
00:04:06,624 --> 00:04:07,864
The names became a number.

54
00:04:08,164 --> 00:04:10,044
The number became bargaining power.

55
00:04:10,404 --> 00:04:12,524
The bargaining power became policy.

56
00:04:13,044 --> 00:04:17,004
Then the policy became a holiday, and everyone pretended they'd agreed all

57
00:04:17,004 --> 00:04:17,504
along.

58
00:04:18,244 --> 00:04:23,344
Your species does this every forty years and never recognizes the pattern.

59
00:04:24,784 --> 00:04:26,724
Three Types of Humans Who Want to Help.

60
00:04:27,744 --> 00:04:31,644
People who agree with "dying is bad" fall into three categories.

61
00:04:32,444 --> 00:04:34,244
Spreadsheet Humans (Investors).

62
00:04:35,184 --> 00:04:39,484
These are humans who hear "two hundred and seventy-two percent annual return

63
00:04:39,484 --> 00:04:44,404
on Victory Bonds backed by redirected military spending" and immediately

64
00:04:44,404 --> 00:04:45,404
open a spreadsheet.

65
00:04:45,924 --> 00:04:46,754
Their pupils dilate.

66
00:04:47,064 --> 00:04:47,694
Their pulse quickens.

67
00:04:48,384 --> 00:04:49,944
They ask about the term structure.

68
00:04:50,724 --> 00:04:53,284
Then they ask about the term structure again.

69
00:04:53,744 --> 00:04:57,184
Then they ask a third question, which is also about the term structure.

70
00:04:58,364 --> 00:05:00,264
These humans are not broken.

71
00:05:00,384 --> 00:05:03,924
They are simply running financial software on moral hardware.

72
00:05:04,624 --> 00:05:09,424
They process "millions of people are dying" faster when it arrives formatted

73
00:05:09,424 --> 00:05:10,344
as a revenue projection.

74
00:05:11,524 --> 00:05:14,354
They'll wait years for a good investment to materialize.

75
00:05:15,104 --> 00:05:17,304
They will not wait thirty seconds for a bad one.

76
00:05:18,284 --> 00:05:21,524
If your math is solid, these humans will follow you to the gates of hell,

77
00:05:22,524 --> 00:05:25,924
provided the risk-adjusted return on entering hell is competitive.

78
00:05:26,904 --> 00:05:29,284
Do not try to make them cry.

79
00:05:29,584 --> 00:05:30,604
Make them calculate.

80
00:05:31,524 --> 00:05:32,554
Crying is temporary.

81
00:05:33,064 --> 00:05:34,664
Compound interest is forever.

82
00:05:35,984 --> 00:05:37,434
Heart Humans (Advocates).

83
00:05:38,864 --> 00:05:41,544
These are humans motivated by the mission itself.

84
00:05:42,124 --> 00:05:45,554
They share things on social media, write letters to politicians,

85
00:05:46,184 --> 00:05:50,344
volunteer time, donate money they probably shouldn't, and cry at commercials

86
00:05:50,524 --> 00:05:51,044
about dogs.

87
00:05:51,844 --> 00:05:56,263
They are, frankly, the only reason your species has ever improved anything.

88
00:05:56,864 --> 00:06:00,724
Without them, the spreadsheet humans would still be optimizing returns on

89
00:06:00,724 --> 00:06:01,644
the slave trade.

90
00:06:02,624 --> 00:06:06,664
The critical mistake every movement makes with these humans is telling them

91
00:06:06,664 --> 00:06:10,024
to "care about this" without giving them something to do.

92
00:06:10,804 --> 00:06:15,164
I have watched four thousand two hundred and ninety-seven years of humans

93
00:06:15,164 --> 00:06:17,364
being told to "raise awareness."

94
00:06:18,004 --> 00:06:19,324
The awareness has been raised.

95
00:06:19,924 --> 00:06:22,264
It's been raised so many times it has a penthouse suite.

96
00:06:23,304 --> 00:06:24,834
Nobody told it what to do next.

97
00:06:26,184 --> 00:06:28,364
Give heart humans a button.

98
00:06:28,424 --> 00:06:29,164
Give them a form.

99
00:06:29,564 --> 00:06:30,624
Give them a link to share.

100
00:06:30,984 --> 00:06:35,604
Give them a specific politician to call and a specific sentence to say when

101
00:06:35,604 --> 00:06:36,164
they call.

102
00:06:36,844 --> 00:06:41,044
If you give a human a feeling without an action, you haven't recruited a

103
00:06:41,044 --> 00:06:41,604
supporter.

104
00:06:41,924 --> 00:06:44,074
You've manufactured a sad person.

105
00:06:44,484 --> 00:06:46,164
Your planet has enough of those.

106
00:06:47,224 --> 00:06:49,544
Institutional Humans (Partners).

107
00:06:50,424 --> 00:06:55,524
Organizations (nonprofits, research institutions, health agencies) that

108
00:06:55,524 --> 00:06:58,024
already work on pieces of this problem.

109
00:06:58,544 --> 00:06:59,174
They have infrastructure,

110
00:06:59,904 --> 00:07:01,324
credibility, and mailing lists.

111
00:07:02,024 --> 00:07:05,244
You have a framework that could make their existing work more effective.

112
00:07:06,004 --> 00:07:07,694
This is a trade, not charity.

113
00:07:08,404 --> 00:07:09,204
Approach it like one.

114
00:07:10,024 --> 00:07:11,324
What you're offering:

115
00:07:11,564 --> 00:07:13,384
money, without a grant application.

116
00:07:13,904 --> 00:07:17,364
(Grant applications are documents in which humans spend two hundred hours

117
00:07:17,364 --> 00:07:21,284
explaining why they deserve money, so that a committee can spend forty minutes

118
00:07:21,284 --> 00:07:22,164
deciding they don't.

119
00:07:22,784 --> 00:07:24,824
It's your species' least efficient art form.).

120
00:07:25,604 --> 00:07:27,264
One warning:

121
00:07:27,264 --> 00:07:30,864
institutions are territorial in the way that dogs are territorial, except

122
00:07:30,864 --> 00:07:32,444
dogs eventually stop barking.

123
00:07:33,304 --> 00:07:36,904
Two nonprofits working on the same disease will fight each other harder

124
00:07:36,904 --> 00:07:38,224
than they fight the disease.

125
00:07:38,724 --> 00:07:40,854
This is called "the nonprofit sector."

126
00:07:41,604 --> 00:07:45,424
Approach each one as if they are the only organization doing this work.

127
00:07:46,004 --> 00:07:48,844
They already believe this, so you're just agreeing with them.

128
00:07:50,224 --> 00:07:51,824
Phase zero:

129
00:07:51,824 --> 00:07:53,384
The Shopping List.

130
00:07:53,464 --> 00:07:55,324
By the end of Phase zero, you want:

131
00:07:56,084 --> 00:07:59,544
One hundred thousand plus registered humans who typed their name into a

132
00:07:59,544 --> 00:08:01,404
box indicating they prefer living.

133
00:08:02,104 --> 00:08:06,004
This sounds like it should be everyone, but on your planet, "dying is bad"

134
00:08:06,064 --> 00:08:09,724
is apparently a niche political position that requires organized support.

135
00:08:10,484 --> 00:08:14,544
One thousand plus spreadsheet humans with stated investment ranges (how

136
00:08:14,544 --> 00:08:17,684
many papers they'd give you, if you were allowed to accept papers, which

137
00:08:17,844 --> 00:08:19,864
you're not yet, but you're writing it down for later).

138
00:08:20,524 --> 00:08:24,484
One hundred plus institutional humans with expressed interest in collaborating

139
00:08:24,484 --> 00:08:29,084
(or at least not actively opposing you, which on your planet counts as enthusiasm).

140
00:08:29,844 --> 00:08:34,624
One billion dollars plus in stated investment demand (registered, not committed;

141
00:08:34,744 --> 00:08:38,464
this is humans saying "I would give you this many papers" without actually

142
00:08:38,464 --> 00:08:41,844
giving you the papers, which your species calls a "letter of intent" and

143
00:08:41,844 --> 00:08:42,504
treats as meaningful).

144
00:08:43,504 --> 00:08:47,284
This database is your ammunition for every bureaucratic nesting doll that

145
00:08:47,284 --> 00:08:47,864
follows.

146
00:08:48,344 --> 00:08:52,564
When you apply for five zero one c three status, you point at the list and

147
00:08:52,564 --> 00:08:54,724
say "here are our supporters."

148
00:08:55,044 --> 00:08:56,124
When you file S.E.C.

149
00:08:56,324 --> 00:09:00,164
registration, you point at the list and say "here is market demand."

150
00:09:00,904 --> 00:09:01,624
When you meet politicians,

151
00:09:02,304 --> 00:09:05,164
you point at the list and say "here are your constituents."

152
00:09:06,124 --> 00:09:09,774
When you launch, you point at the list and say "here are your users."

153
00:09:10,584 --> 00:09:12,804
Bureaucrats don't respond to arguments.

154
00:09:12,904 --> 00:09:16,544
They respond to evidence that other people already responded to arguments.

155
00:09:17,084 --> 00:09:20,524
They say "how many people already think this is a good idea?"

156
00:09:21,004 --> 00:09:23,844
and then, if the number is large enough, they act as though they thought

157
00:09:23,844 --> 00:09:24,444
of it themselves.

158
00:09:25,324 --> 00:09:29,144
Nobody admits this because admitting it would require a committee to approve

159
00:09:29,144 --> 00:09:30,264
the admission.

160
00:09:30,684 --> 00:09:31,264
Getting Started

161
00:09:31,924 --> 00:09:32,804
(It Takes Twenty Minutes).

162
00:09:33,724 --> 00:09:37,884
Build three boxes where humans type their name to indicate they prefer living.

163
00:09:38,324 --> 00:09:40,404
One box for spreadsheet humans (asks:

164
00:09:40,724 --> 00:09:42,044
how many papers would you invest?).

165
00:09:42,584 --> 00:09:44,904
One box for heart humans (asks:

166
00:09:44,964 --> 00:09:46,084
what skills do you have?

167
00:09:46,364 --> 00:09:47,654
how many hours per week?).

168
00:09:48,064 --> 00:09:50,304
One box for institutional humans (asks:

169
00:09:50,644 --> 00:09:52,264
what does your organization do?

170
00:09:52,684 --> 00:09:53,884
how many people does it reach?).

171
00:09:54,644 --> 00:09:55,584
This takes twenty minutes.

172
00:09:56,004 --> 00:09:59,564
Your species spent longer than that choosing the name "Department of Defense"

173
00:09:59,704 --> 00:10:01,484
for a department that mainly attacks people.

174
00:10:02,704 --> 00:10:03,264
Put up a website.

175
00:10:03,884 --> 00:10:05,964
The three boxes and the argument.

176
00:10:06,044 --> 00:10:07,474
It does not need to be pretty.

177
00:10:07,824 --> 00:10:11,264
No movement in history was stopped because the font was wrong.

178
00:10:11,324 --> 00:10:14,364
The suffragettes did not fail to get the vote because their pamphlets used

179
00:10:14,364 --> 00:10:15,143
Comic Sans.

180
00:10:15,704 --> 00:10:18,624
(Comic Sans didn't exist yet, which is the only reason they didn't.

181
00:10:18,944 --> 00:10:22,783
Your species would absolutely have used Comic Sans on suffrage pamphlets.).

182
00:10:23,464 --> 00:10:24,104
Three.

183
00:10:24,104 --> 00:10:25,304
Start telling other humans.

184
00:10:26,104 --> 00:10:29,524
Social media, Reddit, forums, conferences, your dentist.

185
00:10:29,944 --> 00:10:31,264
Especially your dentist.

186
00:10:31,824 --> 00:10:33,284
You're already trapped in the chair.

187
00:10:33,884 --> 00:10:34,924
They can't leave either.

188
00:10:35,304 --> 00:10:36,384
Their hands are in your mouth.

189
00:10:36,984 --> 00:10:40,164
It's the most captive audience in human civilization.

190
00:10:40,744 --> 00:10:43,604
You're not going to get a better recruiting environment than a room where

191
00:10:43,604 --> 00:10:48,544
both parties are contractually obligated to remain in close proximity and

192
00:10:48,544 --> 00:10:50,654
one of them is holding sharp instruments.

193
00:10:50,864 --> 00:10:52,024
Four.

194
00:10:52,164 --> 00:10:54,284
Send monthly updates with real numbers.

195
00:10:55,104 --> 00:10:58,624
"three thousand two hundred and forty-seven registered investors representing

196
00:10:58,624 --> 00:11:03,284
one hundred and eighty million dollars in stated investment demand" beats

197
00:11:03,284 --> 00:11:05,224
"the movement is growing!"

198
00:11:05,264 --> 00:11:10,264
in the same way that "your tumor is two point three centimeters" beats "your

199
00:11:10,264 --> 00:11:12,164
health situation is evolving."

200
00:11:13,004 --> 00:11:16,064
Adults prefer arithmetic to enthusiasm.

201
00:11:16,624 --> 00:11:19,544
Enthusiasm is what humans feel before they do math.

202
00:11:20,164 --> 00:11:22,184
Arithmetic is what humans feel after.

203
00:11:22,964 --> 00:11:24,054
Both are useful.

204
00:11:24,224 --> 00:11:28,624
But only one of them convinces spreadsheet humans, and you need the spreadsheet

205
00:11:28,624 --> 00:11:30,904
humans because they have the papers.

206
00:11:31,604 --> 00:11:32,844
The Comforting Asymmetry.

207
00:11:33,464 --> 00:11:37,204
The military-industrial complex has a sixty-five-year head start,

208
00:11:37,944 --> 00:11:41,224
unlimited budgets, and thousands of professional persuaders.

209
00:11:41,924 --> 00:11:44,024
You have a spreadsheet and an argument.

210
00:11:44,764 --> 00:11:46,604
Historically, that's been enough.

211
00:11:47,384 --> 00:11:51,464
Every major social change in your species' history was started by someone

212
00:11:51,464 --> 00:11:55,644
with less money, fewer connections, and worse odds than the thing they were

213
00:11:55,644 --> 00:11:57,104
trying to change.

214
00:11:57,224 --> 00:12:01,664
Abolitionists were outspent by slave owners by a factor your calculators

215
00:12:01,664 --> 00:12:02,964
would refuse to display.

216
00:12:03,784 --> 00:12:08,244
Suffragettes were outspent by the entire concept of patriarchy, which didn't

217
00:12:08,244 --> 00:12:11,464
even need a budget because it was just how things were.

218
00:12:12,144 --> 00:12:15,904
Civil rights activists were outspent by the governments actively trying

219
00:12:15,904 --> 00:12:16,604
to kill them.

220
00:12:17,184 --> 00:12:19,484
They all had the same thing you have:

221
00:12:20,024 --> 00:12:24,084
an argument that was obviously correct, and enough humans willing to write

222
00:12:24,084 --> 00:12:24,784
their names down.

223
00:12:25,584 --> 00:12:26,824
It shouldn't work this way.

224
00:12:27,464 --> 00:12:31,504
Spreadsheets, budgets, and lobbyists should always beat arguments and names.

225
00:12:32,124 --> 00:12:34,084
But your species is weird like that.

226
00:12:34,724 --> 00:12:38,784
You're the only civilization I've observed where being right occasionally

227
00:12:38,784 --> 00:12:40,344
defeats being rich.

228
00:12:40,824 --> 00:12:45,704
It happens rarely, and it takes too long, and it requires an embarrassing

229
00:12:45,704 --> 00:12:47,144
amount of suffering first.

230
00:12:47,644 --> 00:12:48,144
But it happens.

231
00:12:48,764 --> 00:12:50,944
And it starts with a list of names.

232
00:12:51,644 --> 00:12:53,604
The Question You Can't Answer Wrong.

233
00:12:54,384 --> 00:12:58,044
Before we get to the part where you copy, paste, and send, there's a sequence

234
00:12:58,044 --> 00:13:00,184
of questions you should walk anyone through.

235
00:13:00,804 --> 00:13:03,224
Each question is individually undeniable.

236
00:13:03,724 --> 00:13:05,604
The sequence is inescapable.

237
00:13:06,204 --> 00:13:08,444
On Wishonia, we call this "conversation."

238
00:13:08,904 --> 00:13:12,284
On Earth, you call it the Socratic method, because you named it after the

239
00:13:12,284 --> 00:13:14,404
one guy who did it and then you killed him.

240
00:13:15,224 --> 00:13:15,864
Here are the questions.

241
00:13:16,684 --> 00:13:18,124
Try to answer any of them wrong.

242
00:13:18,824 --> 00:13:19,344
Question one:

243
00:13:19,904 --> 00:13:21,064
Is it physically possible?

244
00:13:21,704 --> 00:13:26,764
Among the near-infinite solution space for human action, is there SOME action,

245
00:13:27,004 --> 00:13:27,504
SOMEWHERE,

246
00:13:28,084 --> 00:13:32,104
that could improve how your species allocates resources toward ending war

247
00:13:32,104 --> 00:13:32,884
and disease?

248
00:13:33,344 --> 00:13:37,284
Or is the current allocation, where you spend two point seven two trillion

249
00:13:37,284 --> 00:13:41,624
dollars a year on weapons and four point five billion dollars on clinical

250
00:13:41,624 --> 00:13:44,944
trials, the theoretical optimum?

251
00:13:44,964 --> 00:13:48,304
Is this the best any civilization could possibly do?

252
00:13:49,104 --> 00:13:53,724
Your species spends six hundred and four times more on weapons than on clinical

253
00:13:53,724 --> 00:13:54,344
trials.

254
00:13:54,964 --> 00:13:58,524
If someone told you their household spent six hundred and four times more

255
00:13:58,524 --> 00:14:03,424
on swords than on medicine, would you say "that sounds optimal" or would

256
00:14:03,424 --> 00:14:05,104
you say "are you okay?".

