299
00:16:09,644 --> 00:16:11,204
You would be bad at math.

300
00:16:12,244 --> 00:16:12,744
Question five:

301
00:16:13,544 --> 00:16:14,484
Then what are you waiting for?

302
00:16:15,484 --> 00:16:19,964
If ending war and disease is physically possible, and all humans would benefit

303
00:16:19,964 --> 00:16:21,724
unimaginably from it,

304
00:16:22,344 --> 00:16:24,964
then you don't need to persuade anyone to be altruistic.

305
00:16:25,784 --> 00:16:28,444
You need to get the argument in front of one credible,

306
00:16:29,164 --> 00:16:33,024
self-interested actor with enough capital and legitimacy to trigger the

307
00:16:33,024 --> 00:16:34,164
financing mechanism.

308
00:16:34,744 --> 00:16:38,864
In practice, that means one person who can publicly underwrite the assurance

309
00:16:38,864 --> 00:16:39,524
contract,

310
00:16:40,224 --> 00:16:44,664
fund the initial bonus pool, and make everyone after them feel less crazy.

311
00:16:45,324 --> 00:16:49,004
In a world where that person understood the compounding benefits and the

312
00:16:49,004 --> 00:16:52,964
mechanism, the end of war and disease would not require heroism.

313
00:16:53,604 --> 00:16:55,104
It would require arithmetic.

314
00:16:56,004 --> 00:16:57,004
That is the bottleneck.

315
00:16:57,504 --> 00:16:59,424
Not generic "awareness."

316
00:16:59,424 --> 00:17:01,484
Not funding in the aggregate.

317
00:17:01,504 --> 00:17:02,644
Not human nature.

318
00:17:03,204 --> 00:17:06,744
The bottleneck is that nobody with a large enough checkbook has read this

319
00:17:06,744 --> 00:17:07,244
yet.

320
00:17:07,744 --> 00:17:12,464
The entire apparatus of self-interest is sitting there, ready to work, waiting

321
00:17:12,464 --> 00:17:17,184
for one public commitment that has not happened yet because someone in the

322
00:17:17,184 --> 00:17:18,784
chain decided they were "busy.".

323
00:17:19,764 --> 00:17:23,684
On Wishonia, this sequence of logic doesn't have a name, for the same reason

324
00:17:23,684 --> 00:17:25,904
gravity doesn't have a marketing department.

325
00:17:26,484 --> 00:17:30,464
On Earth, you apparently need to brand obvious things before your species

326
00:17:30,464 --> 00:17:32,544
will take them seriously, so:

327
00:17:33,004 --> 00:17:35,664
The Logical Inevitability Theorem.

328
00:17:35,784 --> 00:17:40,064
If an optimization is physically possible, and its benefits compound for

329
00:17:40,244 --> 00:17:45,244
all participants, then the decisive trigger is one informed self-interested

330
00:17:45,244 --> 00:17:48,364
first mover making a credible public commitment.

331
00:17:49,044 --> 00:17:50,444
After that, it spreads.

332
00:17:50,904 --> 00:17:51,404
That's it.

333
00:17:51,764 --> 00:17:52,344
That's the theorem.

334
00:17:52,984 --> 00:17:54,284
Five sentences.

335
00:17:54,364 --> 00:17:57,784
On Wishonia, this is considered too obvious to state.

336
00:17:58,324 --> 00:18:01,524
On Earth, it's considered too idealistic to believe.

337
00:18:02,324 --> 00:18:03,804
One of these planets cured disease.

338
00:18:04,424 --> 00:18:06,404
The other one is still arguing about it.

339
00:18:07,144 --> 00:18:11,084
On Wishonia, the Logical Inevitability Theorem would take about four minutes

340
00:18:11,084 --> 00:18:14,704
to demonstrate and the conversation would end with both parties agreeing

341
00:18:14,704 --> 00:18:16,584
to stop wasting money on murder.

342
00:18:17,184 --> 00:18:21,004
On Earth, it takes four minutes and the conversation ends with one party

343
00:18:21,004 --> 00:18:24,884
saying "interesting, I'll think about it" and then never thinking about

344
00:18:24,884 --> 00:18:25,384
it.

345
00:18:25,844 --> 00:18:29,184
This is the coordination failure the entire manual is about.

346
00:18:29,804 --> 00:18:31,504
You are not reading about it.

347
00:18:31,724 --> 00:18:33,324
You are currently doing it.

348
00:18:34,824 --> 00:18:40,084
The Zero Percent Problem Most humans do not refute novel proposals.

349
00:18:40,504 --> 00:18:43,644
They round them down to zero and call that discernment.

350
00:18:44,224 --> 00:18:46,484
But zero percent is not a mood.

351
00:18:46,744 --> 00:18:47,484
It is a claim.

352
00:18:48,164 --> 00:18:52,624
To assign literal zero probability to this plan, you need to assert at least

353
00:18:52,624 --> 00:18:53,984
one of the following:

354
00:18:54,624 --> 00:18:57,704
Better global resource allocation is physically impossible.

355
00:18:58,364 --> 00:19:01,184
No way of paying people could ever change politics.

356
00:19:01,884 --> 00:19:05,764
This specific mechanism has a fatal flaw you can name.

357
00:19:05,764 --> 00:19:09,624
If you are not claiming one of those three things, then your actual estimate

358
00:19:09,624 --> 00:19:11,364
is not zero percent.

359
00:19:11,384 --> 00:19:13,544
It is "I have not evaluated it."

360
00:19:14,064 --> 00:19:15,814
That is a different sentence.

361
00:19:16,464 --> 00:19:21,224
And once the probability is above zero by any nontrivial amount, forwarding

362
00:19:21,224 --> 00:19:24,744
it to one capable evaluator becomes the rational move.

363
00:19:25,324 --> 00:19:26,184
The cost is trivial.

364
00:19:27,084 --> 00:19:28,704
You are not being asked to believe.

365
00:19:29,324 --> 00:19:33,584
You are being asked not to disguise unexamined dismissal as analysis.

366
00:19:34,604 --> 00:19:36,024
How Trivial, Exactly.

367
00:19:36,704 --> 00:19:39,564
On Wishonia, "the cost is trivial" would be sufficient.

368
00:19:40,104 --> 00:19:42,384
On Earth, your species requires a number.

369
00:19:43,444 --> 00:19:45,324
Forwarding takes roughly thirty seconds.

370
00:19:46,044 --> 00:19:49,624
The average human earns seven dollars and nineteen cents per hour.

371
00:19:50,284 --> 00:19:53,724
That makes the opportunity cost of sharing approximately six cents.

372
00:19:54,804 --> 00:19:59,744
The upside, if the treaty path works, is fourteen point nine million dollars

373
00:19:59,744 --> 00:20:04,504
in additional cumulative lifetime income for the average person (from the

374
00:20:04,504 --> 00:20:06,424
compounding math in G.D.P.

375
00:20:06,424 --> 00:20:07,344
Trajectories);

376
00:20:07,584 --> 00:20:09,984
thirteen point five times their current trajectory.

377
00:20:10,944 --> 00:20:15,244
(If you earn more than the global average, your personal gain is proportionally

378
00:20:15,244 --> 00:20:15,744
larger.).

379
00:20:16,924 --> 00:20:21,844
The upside exceeds the downside by a factor of two hundred and forty-eight

380
00:20:21,844 --> 00:20:24,684
point two million times.

381
00:20:24,744 --> 00:20:29,824
Which means sharing is irrational only if the probability of *any* improvement

382
00:20:29,824 --> 00:20:35,184
to global resource allocation is less than one in two hundred and forty-eight

383
00:20:35,184 --> 00:20:35,804
million.

384
00:20:36,704 --> 00:20:37,824
To put that in perspective:

385
00:20:38,244 --> 00:20:42,364
the probability of being struck by lightning in a given year is about one

386
00:20:42,364 --> 00:20:44,024
in one point two million.

387
00:20:44,624 --> 00:20:49,264
You would need to believe this plan is roughly two hundred times less likely

388
00:20:49,264 --> 00:20:51,104
than being struck by lightning.

389
00:20:51,924 --> 00:20:53,344
Not "unlikely."

390
00:20:53,384 --> 00:20:54,584
Not "a long shot."

391
00:20:55,144 --> 00:20:59,604
Two hundred times less likely than a thing that actually happens to real

392
00:20:59,604 --> 00:21:01,184
humans every year.

393
00:21:01,844 --> 00:21:05,404
And note what "this plan working" requires you to deny.

394
00:21:05,884 --> 00:21:09,024
The five questions of the Logical Inevitability Theorem:

395
00:21:09,684 --> 00:21:12,804
Is better resource allocation physically possible?

396
00:21:13,644 --> 00:21:17,264
To get below the breakeven threshold, you'd need to believe it is physically

397
00:21:17,264 --> 00:21:22,264
impossible to improve on a system that spends two point seven two trillion

398
00:21:22,264 --> 00:21:26,704
dollars per year preparing to kill people and sixty billion dollars per

399
00:21:26,704 --> 00:21:27,964
year trying to cure them.

400
00:21:28,804 --> 00:21:30,124
Do the benefits compound?

401
00:21:30,964 --> 00:21:34,884
You'd need to believe that redirecting resources from destruction to medicine

402
00:21:34,884 --> 00:21:39,864
produces zero cumulative economic or health gains over twenty years.

403
00:21:40,324 --> 00:21:41,464
Not small gains.

404
00:21:41,984 --> 00:21:42,484
Zero.

405
00:21:43,264 --> 00:21:45,094
Is there a less-bad approach?

406
00:21:45,884 --> 00:21:49,944
You'd need to believe that no incentive-compatible mechanism, out of all

407
00:21:49,944 --> 00:21:54,024
possible mechanisms, could ever motivate any political shift.

408
00:21:54,684 --> 00:21:56,544
Not this specific mechanism.

409
00:21:57,124 --> 00:21:58,084
Any mechanism.

410
00:21:59,044 --> 00:22:01,124
Does this dominate alternatives?

411
00:22:01,704 --> 00:22:05,744
You'd need to believe that no reallocation of military spending has ever

412
00:22:05,744 --> 00:22:06,244
worked,

413
00:22:06,764 --> 00:22:11,224
despite your own species cutting military spending by eighty-seven percent

414
00:22:11,224 --> 00:22:16,144
after World War Two and experiencing the largest economic boom in human

415
00:22:16,144 --> 00:22:16,724
history.

416
00:22:17,764 --> 00:22:21,184
Is the only bottleneck informed self-interest?

417
00:22:22,024 --> 00:22:26,684
You'd need to believe that no self-interested actor (billionaire, sovereign

418
00:22:26,684 --> 00:22:30,644
wealth fund, or government) would ever act when the return on investment

419
00:22:30,644 --> 00:22:35,304
is eighty-four point eight million to one, even when the structure pays

420
00:22:35,304 --> 00:22:36,324
them to do so.

421
00:22:36,804 --> 00:22:38,404
To clear the breakeven threshold,

422
00:22:40,464 --> 00:22:42,124
you don't need to believe all five.

423
00:22:42,124 --> 00:22:43,604
You need to believe *any one of them* is not impossible.

424
00:22:44,524 --> 00:22:45,304
That's it.

425
00:22:45,504 --> 00:22:49,404
One non-zero answer out of five, and sharing becomes the rational move.

426
00:22:50,024 --> 00:22:51,824
And this calculation is conservative.

427
00:22:52,324 --> 00:22:53,884
It counts only the income gain.

428
00:22:54,364 --> 00:22:58,284
It assigns zero value to the ten point seven billion lives.

429
00:22:58,704 --> 00:23:03,664
It ignores the Wishonia path entirely (which is forty-five times the current

430
00:23:03,664 --> 00:23:05,944
trajectory, not thirteen point five times).

431
00:23:06,944 --> 00:23:10,584
It assumes you personally capture only the average gain, when in practice

432
00:23:10,584 --> 00:23:13,004
higher earners gain proportionally more.

433
00:23:13,584 --> 00:23:17,864
The actual breakeven threshold is even more forgiving than one in two hundred

434
00:23:17,864 --> 00:23:19,284
and forty-eight million.

435
00:23:20,384 --> 00:23:24,344
On Wishonia, a species that couldn't clear a one-in-two hundred and forty-eight

436
00:23:24,344 --> 00:23:29,424
million bar for obvious self-interest would be a genuinely novel research

437
00:23:29,424 --> 00:23:29,924
subject.

438
00:23:30,464 --> 00:23:34,424
We have never encountered a species that fails to act on incentives this

439
00:23:34,424 --> 00:23:35,024
large.

440
00:23:35,624 --> 00:23:36,664
We don't have a word for it.

441
00:23:37,264 --> 00:23:41,304
The closest translation is "sleeping through your own house fire, but on

442
00:23:41,304 --> 00:23:41,804
purpose.".

443
00:23:42,904 --> 00:23:44,324
The Only Remaining Failure Mode.

444
00:23:45,244 --> 00:23:45,744
So:

445
00:23:46,044 --> 00:23:48,864
better resource allocation is physically possible.

446
00:23:48,924 --> 00:23:50,184
The benefits compound.

447
00:23:50,484 --> 00:23:51,864
No better mechanism exists.

448
00:23:52,344 --> 00:23:53,844
The precedent is real.

449
00:23:53,944 --> 00:23:55,544
The incentives pay.

450
00:23:55,584 --> 00:24:00,504
Sharing costs thirty seconds and is rational at any probability above one

451
00:24:00,504 --> 00:24:01,984
in two hundred and forty-eight million.

452
00:24:03,104 --> 00:24:04,614
The math can't be wrong.

453
00:24:04,764 --> 00:24:06,624
The incentives can't fail.

454
00:24:06,764 --> 00:24:08,524
Selfishness can't stop it;

455
00:24:08,684 --> 00:24:10,004
selfishness is the engine.

456
00:24:10,464 --> 00:24:13,964
The only thing that can kill it is you not reading this far and then not

457
00:24:13,964 --> 00:24:14,904
pressing "send."

458
00:24:15,484 --> 00:24:15,984
That's it.

459
00:24:16,404 --> 00:24:20,724
The entire distance between here and the treaty is made of humans who couldn't

460
00:24:20,724 --> 00:24:22,324
